{
  "tagline": "A railroad town named for a joke about Duluth, Minnesota, running from the Chattahoochee to Interstate 85.",
  "summary": "Duluth began as Howell's Crossing and took its name in 1871, when the railroad arrived — borrowed from Duluth, Minnesota, whose own railroad a congressman had just mocked. The city runs south from the Chattahoochee River across the tracks and its Town Green to Interstate 85, Gas South Arena and the old Gwinnett Place Mall, which the county bought in 2020 to rebuild. About 32,000 people live in the city; its schools are Gwinnett County's, and homes north of the river with a Duluth address are in Fulton County.",
  "locationNote": "25 mi northeast of downtown Atlanta",
